
# 4. SRD — SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS DOCUMENT

# FixMyCampus — System Requirements Document

**Version:** 1.0
**Date:** 06 September 2026

---

# 1. System Purpose

FixMyCampus provides a centralized system for reporting and resolving campus infrastructure problems.

The system ensures that complaints are:

* Recorded
* Assigned
* Processed
* Resolved
* Confirmed
* Closed
* Evaluated

---

# 2. System Actors

| Actor   | Main Permissions                      |
| ------- | ------------------------------------- |
| Student | Create and track own complaints       |
| Staff   | Process assigned complaints           |
| Admin   | Manage all complaints and assignments |

---

# 3. Authentication Requirements

The system shall:

1. Provide user registration.
2. Provide login.
3. Create authenticated sessions.
4. Provide logout.
5. Reject unauthenticated protected requests.

---

# 4. Student Requirements

Students shall be able to:

* Register.
* Login.
* Report complaints.
* View own complaints.
* View complaint details.
* Track status.
* View timeline.
* Communicate with assigned staff.
* Receive notifications.
* Close resolved complaints.
* Submit feedback.

Students shall not be able to:

* Access other students' complaints.
* Access staff-only complaints.
* Access admin functions.
* Close unresolved complaints.

---

# 5. Staff Requirements

Staff shall be able to:

* Login.
* View assigned complaints.
* View complaint details.
* Update status.
* Add remarks.
* Mark complaints Resolved.
* Communicate with complaint owners.

Staff shall not:

* View another staff member's assigned complaints.
* Close complaints.
* Access admin functions.

---

# 6. Admin Requirements

Admins shall be able to:

* Login.
* View all complaints.
* View student information.
* Assign staff.
* View complaint details.
* View complaint history.

---

# 7. Complaint Management

Each complaint shall contain information such as:

* Complaint ID
* Complaint code
* Student
* Category
* Location
* Title
* Description
* Priority
* Status
* Creation time
* Update time
* Resolution time
* Closure time

---

# 8. Assignment Requirements

An administrator shall be able to assign a complaint to an eligible staff member.

Assignment information shall contain:

* Complaint
* Staff
* Admin who assigned it
* Assignment timestamp
* Completion timestamp where applicable

---

# 9. Status Requirements

Supported statuses include:

```text
Submitted
Under Review
Assigned
In Progress
Resolved
Closed
Rejected
Duplicate
```

Normal workflow:

```text
Submitted
↓
Under Review
↓
Assigned
↓
In Progress
↓
Resolved
↓
Closed
```

---

# 10. Resolution Requirements

When staff marks a complaint as:

```text
Resolved
```

the server shall record:

```text
resolved_at
```

The complaint remains available for student confirmation.

---

# 11. Closure Requirements

Only the student who owns the complaint can close it.

Closure is allowed only when:

```text
status = Resolved
```

When closure succeeds:

```text
status = Closed
closed_at = current server time
```

Staff cannot close complaints.

---

# 12. Chat Requirements

Chat shall be linked to a specific complaint.

Only these users can participate:

```text
Complaint Student
+
Currently Assigned Staff
```

The chat shall:

* Display messages.
* Store messages.
* Track read status.
* Support notifications.

After closure:

```text
View history → Allowed
Send new message → Not allowed
```

---

# 13. Notification Requirements

The system shall:

* Store notifications.
* Associate notifications with users.
* Optionally associate notifications with complaints.
* Maintain read/unread status.
* Allow individual notification read operations.
* Allow mark-all-as-read.

---

# 14. Feedback Requirements

Feedback shall be available after closure.

Each feedback record contains:

* Complaint
* Student
* Rating
* Comment
* Created timestamp

Rating range:

```text
1–5
```

Each complaint can have at most one feedback record.

---

# 15. XML Requirements

The system shall:

* Export complaint information as XML.
* Restrict student exports to their own complaints.
* Allow authorized administrators to export complaints.
* Validate XML using XSD.
* Validate XML using DTD.

---

# 16. External Interfaces

### Browser Interface

Users interact through HTML/CSS/JavaScript.

### Backend Interface

JavaScript communicates with PHP endpoints.

### Database Interface

PHP communicates with MySQL.

### XML Interface

PHP generates XML and validates it against XSD and DTD.

---

# 17. System Constraints

* Apache is required for local hosting.
* PHP is required for backend execution.
* MySQL is required for persistence.
* The project targets a local academic/development environment.
* Authorization must remain server-side.

---
